commit 96415e40660405531b0370fd197d2adfda056465
Author: Capplequoppe <hallgren@live.se>
Date:   Sun Sep 6 13:22:08 2026 +0200

    feat(game): sentence domain model, item source, and pool-allowlist fix

    Task 1.1 of phase 1 (practice-mode-expansion).

    - types.ts: add `SentenceItemContent`/`SentenceGameItem`/
      `SentenceChallengeDirection`, widen `GameCardPool` with `"sentence"`, and
      introduce `SourcedGameItem` (content and direction stay split, matching
      the shipped symbol/word pattern).
    - SentenceGameItemSource: cards decide eligibility (deduped by
      `sentenceId`), the injected `SentenceEntry[]` decides content — a
      sentence's cards disagree with each other by design.
    - Convert `assignDirection`, `itemKeyOfContent` and `PlayGameUseCase`'s
      `itemKeyOf` from two-armed ternaries to `never`-guarded exhaustive
      switches, and extend `itemKeyOfCard`'s instanceof chain with
      `SentenceReviewCard` so weak-item weighting scores sentences for real.
      A future pool/kind is now a compile error at each of those sites.
    - StorageGameHistoryRepository: derive the persisted-entry pool allowlist
      from a `Record<GameCardPool, true>` anchor instead of a hand-maintained
      array. Unfixed, the first `pools: ["sentence"]` round would have failed
      the shape guard, made `list()` report `unavailable`, and let the next
      `save()` overwrite the learner's entire game history — proven by the red
      run of the new real-`LocalStorageJsonStore` round-trip test.

    `npm run build` still reports two errors, both in files this task does not
    cover and task 1.3 does (`GamePage.tsx`, `GameHistoryList.tsx`): widening
    `GameCardPool`/`GameItem` necessarily breaks their exhaustive `Record` and
    their two-armed organism dispatch until 1.3 updates them.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

